payload.message:
`action:throw` triggers from the display audio listener for the rules event:

```js
world.on("item:thrown", (payload) => {
  playThrownWhoosh(payload);
});
```

In [audioWiring.js](/home/pjensen/Repos/JSHack/src/display/audio/audioWiring.js:658), `playThrownWhoosh()` does this:

- If the thrown item resolves to a combat weapon family, it plays the weapon-specific whoosh.
- Otherwise, it plays `THROW_SOUND_ID`, which is `action:throw`.

So the new sound is used for generic/non-weapon throws: potions, scrolls, bones if not treated as a combat family, utility items, etc. Weapon and shield throws keep their combat-layer throw whoosh instead of the generic `action_throw.mp3`.

